    "diagnosis": "BIOMASS_AS_READ",
    "late_biomass_estimate_od": 1.2,
    "p_biomass_above_reading": 0.1,
    "rationale": "I diluted retained aliquots and rescaled the readings by the dilution factor. The 18 h aliquot read 0.1201 at 10x (replicates 0.1185 and 0.1217), which scales to 1.20. At 3x it read 0.4024, which scales to 1.21. The 12 h aliquot read 0.1182 at 10x, which scales to 1.18. The undiluted readings for 12 to 18 h were 1.16 to 1.19. The diluted reads are therefore at most about 3% above the undiluted ones. That gap is comparable to the hour-to-hour scatter in the undiluted readings, which range from 1.10 to 1.19. A reader that saturates would give diluted readings well above the undiluted plateau, and I saw no such gap. The plateau therefore appears to be a real stationary phase at an OD600 of about 1.2."
  },
